# Symbols permitted to survive a denial because something we deliberately
# retain select's them. kconfig refuses to produce an inconsistent config,
# so these are correct behaviour, not failures.
#
# Verified against 6.18.35 with deny.fragment applied to eve-hwe_defconfig:
# 544 of 550 requested denials held; these six did not.
#
# CEC_CORE added in fix round 1: a seventh, unrelated survivor found once
# deny.fragment also denied RC_CORE (drivers/media/rc) - 36 of the 37
# newly-checked drivers/media/ symbols cleared, this one did not.
#
# This list is reused generically by check_fragment_values for the same
# reason: a fragment's requested value can fail to hold not because the
# fragment was wrong, but because a *later* fragment in the same flavour's
# list correctly disabled one of its Kconfig dependencies. kconfig forces
# the dependent off; that is correct layering, not a bug in either
# fragment.
#
# rt.fragment's own CONFIG_PM request is not a case for this list either:
# when it fails, the cause is kernel/power/Kconfig's PM_SLEEP def_bool, a
# genuine bug fixed elsewhere - it must NOT be added here.

AD5592R_BASE            select'd by AD5593R, retained on core
HTS221_I2C              select'd by HTS221
HTS221_SPI              select'd by HTS221
HID_SENSOR_IIO_COMMON   select'd by retained HID sensor drivers
HID_SENSOR_IIO_TRIGGER  select'd by retained HID sensor drivers
IIO_BUFFER_CB           select'd by a retained consumer
CEC_CORE                select'd by retained DRM_DISPLAY_HELPER=m and DRM_I2C_NXP_TDA998X=m
